  "body": "## Full affirmative solution: initial omnific models of discrete initial groups\n\nEvery discrete initial ordered additive subgroup of No is order-group-isomorphic onto an H contained in Oz that is initial in No. This is the complete set/proper-class target in NBG with global choice, with zero separately included, no multiplication assumption and no simplicity-preservation requirement. The actual normal-form image is used, with no full Hahn completion.\n\nThe original sign-map construction is unchanged. A detailed new dependency supplement repairs two literal details in the imported initial-group characterization proof: cofinal-support exhaustion and legal limit-cut options. It supplies a direct additive cut-adjunction proof, finite monomials first, all actual limit-length supports next, unit rather than potentially unavailable dyadic options, and the class-to-set restriction. The exact full-ray inverse and actual coefficient membership are explicit.\n\nRoot and three fresh full mathematical approaches verified the target; a fourth focused dependency reviewer independently reconstructed the imported sufficiency. Its mechanism exposure is disclosed, not treated as a fourth blind whole-candidate review. Three fresh priority approaches plus root found no earlier recorded full target in inspected accessible bodies. EK2018 least-positive/characterization, ADH negative-ordinal minimum and KKS generic exponent/coefficient transport receive explicit credit. The2024 handbook chapter and other fulltexts remain unread leads; no firstness, novelty, causal-independence or continued-global-openness certificate is asserted.\n\nThe current13-file edition contains operative proof and dependency supplement, actual finite diagnostic program and baseline, and a manifest verifier. Two complete normal/optimized positive outputs and eight actual wrong-construction failures are reproduced. Historical reports are labelled superseded and their absent old programs are not claimed as freshly rerun. Original inputs remain at heada10129f4c09a87460642c36284f300d46d419cab.\n\nAll work is extensively AI-assisted and unrefereed. Internal AI review is not external human peer review, journal acceptance or formal certification. Whole-package preprint review, production publication, tracker and merge are separate gates. The PR remains draft while the package is prepared.\n\n## Exact current file identities\n\n- `ACCEPTANCE.json`: 1553 bytes; SHA-256 `a61bcbd5ab7c28bc4a095655b8f5271146862e90b0a3bed1b3b98a0530065d04`.\n- `ACCEPTANCE.md`: 5531 bytes; SHA-256 `72b0307401792f781ca364638279a73dcdb4d74a7bf500c4a11fdcc72ff06d22`.\n- `AUDIT_REPORT.md`: 15025 bytes; SHA-256 `85f03be9daea4d451e6fec16f4b69a0b2b0a2c97a4c5ed0239654c573ef92909`.\n- `CURRENT_REVIEW.md`: 3002 bytes; SHA-256 `973219cc711b54f8dca2643192e087409868579af5eaec471f4705b7bdcbdcc1`.\n- `DEPENDENCY_PROOF.md`: 10674 bytes; SHA-256 `01858abdf9e2bfc06d7b444400cdbabedc1c09363c167c83dc589e2dee2aa53b`.\n- `EXPECTED_FINITE_SIGNS.json`: 319 bytes; SHA-256 `293ad3539a8df71d2bc0fe31bb2ae09a0154755424cd148a55c13e10276632c2`.\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 2421 bytes; SHA-256 `dcefe1269cdc19b4f081b01c0a16ae570536e6b69eb785945511d1acd3e877be`.\n- `PROOF.md`: 12349 bytes; SHA-256 `4e17b70cf504e7f4f8bf5298df0334de1812387a4e8dfee240b81693542fa5fa`.\n- `README.md`: 1448 bytes; SHA-256 `87a0286ff65a18233311aaa82fe171db2c441dcc6b444868af04d102a0063f3a`.\n- `SOURCE_METADATA.json`: 5129 bytes; SHA-256 `dd914bb2f064e3cf551a711b4080d2a30348cbcedf6ccb948c626d546b90bd3e`.\n- `VERIFICATION_SUMMARY.md`: 1157 bytes; SHA-256 `c7ed7e1487f3b5991d391afa08f114d6a3863fd2385c08c41deae68b45513e90`.\n- `verify_finite_signs.py`: 4625 bytes; SHA-256 `b1c530b47c4477d97d2a419702231b77d49ce9bdf841089998c97cee1e2235b9`.\n- `verify_release.py`: 2090 bytes; SHA-256 `01ea9e88715abd123b6d4d455a7d340ce2e25f749219d37e6baf75df6c7bfc9f`.\n",
